WEBVTT

00:01:35.530 --> 00:01:37.610
Gordon is a very proud steam engine.

00:01:38.140 --> 00:01:40.680
He's the fastest engine on the island of Sodor.

00:01:41.150 --> 00:01:45.490
He loves speeding along his line with the wind blowing across his funnel.

00:01:48.650 --> 00:01:50.770
You've broken the record again, said his driver.

00:01:51.110 --> 00:01:53.210
I'm the fastest, boasted Gordon.

00:01:53.620 --> 00:01:55.380
But not all the engines were impressed.

00:01:56.060 --> 00:01:58.560
Speed isn't everything, said James smugly.

00:01:59.200 --> 00:01:59.980
But being reliable...

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:06.440
and useful is said thomas you slow engines will never understand snorted gordon because you'll

00:02:06.440 --> 00:02:14.280
never go as fast as me sir topham had arrived with news of a special for thomas i want you to

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:21.520
collect a jet engine and take it to the airfield what's a jet engine asked percy a jet engine

00:02:21.520 --> 00:02:26.970
goes forward by pushing hot air out of its back sir topham had explained just like when you blow

00:02:26.970 --> 00:02:29.960
up a balloon and let it go added thomas it's very

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:38.050
very fast. Thomas likes making special deliveries for Sir Topham Hatt. It makes him feel special,

00:02:38.600 --> 00:02:47.050
but secretly, he wished he could go as fast as Gordon. Just once, Thomas arrived at the

00:02:47.050 --> 00:02:56.330
docks excited to see the jet engine. It was shiny and modern, and Thomas had never seen

00:02:56.330 --> 00:02:59.380
anything like it. Couldn't wait to start his journey.

00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:01.640
Cranky was taking his time.

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:05.550
Hurry up, Huff Thomas.

00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:07.360
This is a special, special.

00:03:09.390 --> 00:03:13.110
Cranky did not like being told what to do, especially by an engine.

00:03:14.130 --> 00:03:17.350
He became so cranky that he was careless with his hook.

00:03:18.120 --> 00:03:22.380
His hook knocked the switch, and the switch started the jet engine.

00:03:22.630 --> 00:03:24.910
And the engine began to whine.

00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:28.900
The whining got louder and louder and louder.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:32.000
said Cranky. Before he could

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:33.980
say anything else, the jet engine

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:35.900
was rocketing Thomas up the

00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:38.830
track. Whoa! said

00:03:38.830 --> 00:03:39.290
Thomas.

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:44.050
Driver tried to put on the brakes,

00:03:44.270 --> 00:03:45.970
but Thomas couldn't stop.

00:03:46.290 --> 00:03:47.810
Whoa! Boy!

00:03:48.860 --> 00:03:50.600
The station master called ahead.

00:03:50.740 --> 00:03:56.250
Clear the lines! It's a runaway train!

00:03:58.340 --> 00:03:59.340
Signals were changed.

00:04:00.030 --> 00:04:10.150
and points were switched thomas had never been so excited thomas flew by james and rocketed past

00:04:10.150 --> 00:04:23.830
henry and raced by percy they were amazed birdie was excited when he saw thomas flying down the

00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:26.710
track wanna race thomas beeped birdie

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:33.550
Never mind. No one had ever seen an engine go so fast.

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:42.640
Gordon had no idea that Thomas was racing along the main line.

00:04:50.040 --> 00:04:52.140
I'm the fastest, said Gordon proudly.

00:04:56.330 --> 00:04:59.980
Hi, Gordon. Bye, Gordon. Gordon could not believe...

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:29.920
What he had seen asked the jet engine ran out of fuel Thomas was back under his own power deemed gently back into knapford station sorry for over

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:38.160
taking you back there, Gordon, teased Thomas. Overtake me, I didn't notice, Gordon huffed. You

00:05:38.160 --> 00:05:43.040
didn't notice the fastest engine on the island of Sodor, said Henry. Yes, I am the fastest,

00:05:43.440 --> 00:05:49.460
puffed Thomas. Percy felt a little sorry for Gordon. Gordon doesn't have to go as fast as a

00:05:49.460 --> 00:05:56.840
jet engine. He's a steam engine. But he's still full of hot air, whistled James. And Gordon whished

00:05:56.840 --> 00:05:57.180
away.

00:06:31.180 --> 00:06:42.490
In the summertime, the Branchline Station Masters enjoy a friendly competition for the most beautiful station on the island of Sodor.

00:06:47.770 --> 00:06:49.070
The engines love to help, too.

00:06:51.950 --> 00:06:54.370
One evening, Sir Topham Hatt came to the sheds.

00:06:54.860 --> 00:06:59.520
I want Percy to collect some flower bushes for Lower Tidmouth Station, he said.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:00.900
They're at Mathwaite.

00:07:01.740 --> 00:07:03.120
Mathwaite? Percy said.

00:07:03.640 --> 00:07:05.810
Y-y-yes, sir, he added nervously.

00:07:09.410 --> 00:07:11.890
Percy chuffed anxiously through the thickening fog.

00:07:12.490 --> 00:07:14.650
He doesn't like traveling to Mathwaite at night.

00:07:15.520 --> 00:07:19.840
The line passes through a junction next to a spooky old quarry mine.

00:07:22.830 --> 00:07:25.130
Percy hoped the signal at the junction would be green.

00:07:25.700 --> 00:07:29.470
He didn't want to stop next to the mine, but the signal was red.

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:30.660
He had to stop.

00:07:37.050 --> 00:07:54.300
Suddenly he saw something, bouncing buffers, cried Percy.

00:07:55.100 --> 00:07:58.220
His driver hadn't seen the old chimney sink into the ground.

00:07:59.200 --> 00:07:59.940
The signal changed.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:03.800
Percy was so scared, he steamed away as fast as he could.

00:08:07.060 --> 00:08:10.980
The next day, Percy was telling Donald and Douglas about the disappearing chimney.

00:08:11.470 --> 00:08:13.470
It's the naughty gnomes, teased Donald.

00:08:14.020 --> 00:08:17.680
We fat men with big feet, they make strange things happen, said Douglas.

00:08:18.270 --> 00:08:21.310
It's legend. They steal your wheels and filch your funnels.

00:08:22.810 --> 00:08:25.530
Percy didn't want to believe them, but he wasn't sure.

00:08:28.860 --> 00:08:29.980
Sir Topham Hatt...

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:32.120
was waiting for Percy at Dry Awe Station.

00:08:32.400 --> 00:08:36.120
I want you to collect some freight cars from the abandoned mine, he said.

00:08:36.700 --> 00:08:40.870
Yes, sir, Percy answered, but he really didn't want to go there again.

00:08:44.270 --> 00:08:46.450
Percy hoped he wouldn't see anything else disappear.

00:08:47.230 --> 00:08:50.170
He slipped into the sidings and buffered up to the freight cars.

00:08:52.340 --> 00:08:54.470
Spooky, stammered Percy.

00:08:54.980 --> 00:08:58.640
Suddenly, another building at the old mine sank into the ground.

00:09:09.080 --> 00:09:19.220
was that shouted his driver bouncing buffers shrieked percy he was so scared he lurched

00:09:19.220 --> 00:09:28.170
forward and rammed the freight car naughty gnomes cried percy he steamed away faster than

00:09:28.170 --> 00:09:29.910
before all the way back to

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:38.150
Lower Tidmouth Station. Percy's driver told Sir Topham Hatt what they had seen.

00:09:39.570 --> 00:09:44.230
It's the naughty gnomes, cried Percy. They like to cause trouble. It's legend.

00:09:45.640 --> 00:09:50.620
Nonsense, said Sir Topham Hatt. The old buildings are collapsing into empty mine shafts, that's

00:09:50.620 --> 00:09:57.540
all. But I saw the gnomes, protested Percy. Of course you did, said Sir Topham Hatt. Garden

00:09:57.540 --> 00:09:59.960
gnomes. Garden gnomes?

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:03.960
to decorate Lower Tidmouth Station, Sir Topham Hatt said.

00:10:04.200 --> 00:10:07.480
They're not scary. Garden gnomes bring good luck.

00:10:07.950 --> 00:10:10.830
And he ordered Percy to return immediately and get them.

00:10:10.970 --> 00:10:15.240
Percy was scared, but he knew he had to be responsible, so he carried on.

00:10:16.170 --> 00:10:18.030
I'm not scared. I'm not scared.

00:10:25.090 --> 00:10:29.960
Waited for something else spooky to happen, but it didn't, and Sir Topham Hatt was right.

00:10:30.280 --> 00:10:32.480
The garden gnomes weren't scary at all.

00:10:37.110 --> 00:10:39.570
His driver and fireman had collected the gnomes,

00:10:39.750 --> 00:10:42.490
and Percy took them straight back to Lower Tidmouth Station.

00:10:45.610 --> 00:10:48.170
Later that week, the station master thanked Percy.

00:10:48.650 --> 00:10:51.730
We wouldn't have won our competition without your garden gnomes, Percy.

00:10:53.350 --> 00:10:54.710
Percy was very proud.

00:10:56.880 --> 00:10:59.960
You were right, sir. Naughty gnomes can be lucky after all.

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:00.200
Whoa.

00:11:35.500 --> 00:11:38.360
Engines on the island of Sodor look forward to Halloween.

00:11:40.150 --> 00:11:42.050
They love Sir Topham Hatt's fireworks,

00:11:44.410 --> 00:11:46.630
children dressing up as wizards and witches.

00:11:46.890 --> 00:11:52.040
They also love Edward's spooky stories.

00:11:55.940 --> 00:11:57.400
They say that on Halloween,

00:11:58.020 --> 00:11:59.960
the ghost engine returns to the Sodor

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:02.140
Smelter's looking for his lost whistle.

00:12:05.070 --> 00:12:09.050
Ah, spooky, the engine said, all shivering a little.

00:12:10.740 --> 00:12:12.280
Later, Sir Topham had arrived.

00:12:12.960 --> 00:12:16.440
Thomas, Percy and Duck, I have a special job for you.

00:12:17.250 --> 00:12:19.930
You want to collect some scrap from the Smelter's Yard tonight.

00:12:20.700 --> 00:12:21.440
On Halloween?

00:12:22.980 --> 00:12:23.640
Don't worry.

00:12:23.960 --> 00:12:25.880
You'll be back in time for the fireworks.

00:12:26.370 --> 00:12:29.190
Percy isn't worried about missing the fireworks, teased Thomas.

00:12:29.410 --> 00:12:29.970
He's a sc...

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:40.760
scaredy engine. I am not called Percy, but he was a little. At the Smelters, all Percy could think

00:12:40.760 --> 00:12:50.590
about was Edward's ghost engine. Thomas knew Percy was scared, so he teased him even more.

00:12:51.260 --> 00:12:57.590
What's that up there? Thomas squeaked. Is it a spook? It's just a piece of twisted scrap,

00:12:57.930 --> 00:12:59.010
Percy said nervously.

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:04.060
Isn't it? Thomas was having fun. He kept on teasing Percy.

00:13:04.740 --> 00:13:07.500
Careful the ghost engine doesn't get you, Thomas said.

00:13:07.780 --> 00:13:10.340
There's no such thing as ghosts, snapped Percy.

00:13:12.880 --> 00:13:14.380
Duck felt sorry for Percy.

00:13:15.700 --> 00:13:17.680
Nobody's brave all the time, said Duck.

00:13:18.040 --> 00:13:20.620
But I'm not a scaredy engine, Percy insisted.

00:13:21.930 --> 00:13:25.080
The job was nearly complete.

00:13:25.820 --> 00:13:27.400
Well done, the yard manager said.

00:13:27.860 --> 00:13:29.800
Now I'll need one engine to finish up.

00:13:30.510 --> 00:13:36.640
duck wanted to pay thomas back for all his teasing please sir he said i'm sure thomas wouldn't mind

00:13:36.640 --> 00:13:42.540
staying of course not thomas boasted i'm not a scaredy engine so duck and percy left

00:13:44.390 --> 00:13:55.360
when thomas was by himself every sound and every shadow was spooky

00:14:00.480 --> 00:14:02.480
He was beginning to feel very scared.

00:14:03.150 --> 00:14:05.950
There's no such thing as ghosts, he said nervously.

00:14:06.380 --> 00:14:06.840
Who's there?

00:14:07.560 --> 00:14:11.420
Thomas was so busy looking for ghosts, he didn't watch where he was going.

00:14:20.660 --> 00:14:22.620
Chains felt like ghost fingers.

00:14:23.800 --> 00:14:25.040
Something's got me!

00:14:25.980 --> 00:14:29.080
Thomas whished and set off an old steam whistle.

00:14:33.570 --> 00:14:38.700
Whistle, said Thomas, and he raced away as fast as his wheels could carry him.

00:14:41.950 --> 00:14:43.910
Ghost engine is after me.

00:14:47.160 --> 00:14:50.120
It was naughty of Thomas to tease you, Percy, said Duck.

00:14:50.680 --> 00:14:52.260
He was only playing, said Percy.

00:14:52.480 --> 00:14:53.620
I hope he hurries up.

00:14:53.830 --> 00:14:55.770
I wouldn't want him to be late for the fireworks.

00:14:57.070 --> 00:14:58.350
He's after me.

00:15:00.120 --> 00:15:01.400
I don't think you'll be late, said Duck.

00:15:05.660 --> 00:15:08.440
Duck and Percy joined the other engines for the fireworks.

00:15:12.100 --> 00:15:13.740
Where's Thomas? Percy asked.

00:15:13.960 --> 00:15:15.060
He'll miss all the fun.

00:15:15.520 --> 00:15:18.580
It would serve him right after all his teasing, Duck said.

00:15:19.200 --> 00:15:20.260
But Percy was worried.

00:15:22.590 --> 00:15:23.810
He went to look for his friend.

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:32.420
He found Thomas all alone in the shed.

00:15:33.000 --> 00:15:35.000
Are you all right, Thomas? He said.

00:15:36.260 --> 00:15:39.880
Yes. I'm sorry I teased you, Percy, Thomas said.

00:15:40.120 --> 00:15:42.990
Duck was right. We all feel scared sometimes.

00:15:43.850 --> 00:15:47.130
And we all have to say sorry sometimes, said his friend.

00:15:47.520 --> 00:15:51.100
So come on, Thomas. We can watch the fireworks just as well from here.

00:15:51.300 --> 00:15:56.090
He was right.

00:16:01.240 --> 00:16:01.440
Thank you.

00:16:33.360 --> 00:16:37.000
Harold the helicopter is glad not to be a steam engine.

00:16:38.160 --> 00:16:44.620
He is much happier flying in the sky than racing along on road or rails.

00:16:50.890 --> 00:16:56.420
One sunny morning, the engines were busy preparing for the Vickers' annual garden party.

00:16:58.650 --> 00:16:59.710
I'd like to help!

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:09.500
called Harold. But I'm on patrol! He was looking for engines that might be in trouble.

00:17:14.830 --> 00:17:25.160
Meanwhile, the engines puffed to and fro with their loads for the party. Percy was delivering

00:17:25.160 --> 00:17:29.760
deck chairs and decorations, tables and tea urns, and reminders.

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:32.820
Don't forget to come to the vicar's party!

00:17:34.410 --> 00:17:36.890
Thanks for the invitation, called Harold.

00:17:37.940 --> 00:17:40.840
But duty calls, and he whirred away.

00:17:44.000 --> 00:17:51.600
Harold was landing at his airfield to get more fuel when he saw Pegasus, the cart horse that lives close by.

00:17:52.490 --> 00:17:54.910
Pegasus was getting ready to give rides to children.

00:17:56.260 --> 00:17:59.960
He had a shiny leather harness and a freshly painted car.

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:07.900
Harold was beginning to feel left out of the celebrations.

00:18:08.940 --> 00:18:11.840
He wished more than ever that he could help.

00:18:13.680 --> 00:18:15.740
Thomas puffed in with some passengers.

00:18:18.360 --> 00:18:20.440
Where are you going next? buzzed Harold.

00:18:22.000 --> 00:18:25.310
To the vicar's party, of course. Everyone's going.

00:18:27.740 --> 00:18:29.980
Everyone except me, replied Harold.

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:37.120
Harold I'm on duty yes indeed said Thomas kindly being a rescue helicopter

00:18:37.120 --> 00:18:51.150
is important work but no one needs rescuing side Harold then came the

00:18:51.150 --> 00:18:56.560
surprise Harold's pilot received an urgent call from Sir Topham Hatt

00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:05.660
Pegasus is stuck in a ditch. If he doesn't get to the vicar's party, the children will be disappointed.

00:19:06.390 --> 00:19:09.070
You must rescue him at once.

00:19:10.100 --> 00:19:12.660
All set and ready for action, reported Harold.

00:19:15.240 --> 00:19:18.530
Pegasus, wondered Percy. That's a funny name for a horse.

00:19:19.910 --> 00:19:25.720
It's the name of a flying horse in a very old story, explained Sir Topham Hatt.

00:19:26.490 --> 00:19:29.970
Flying horse, exclaimed Percy. Horses can't fly.

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:43.950
fly? He felt very clever. Harold flew to the rescue as fast as he could. What happened? He asked

00:19:43.950 --> 00:19:53.090
Thomas. We were loading the cart. Pegasus wandered off into the ditch. Silly horse. Now he's stuck.

00:19:53.850 --> 00:19:59.050
If you can take him, I can take the cart. I'll put Pegasus in my sling.

00:20:00.540 --> 00:20:02.360
We need to hurry, whistled Thomas.

00:20:02.740 --> 00:20:04.300
The party is about to begin.

00:20:05.090 --> 00:20:06.350
And he steamed away.

00:20:10.110 --> 00:20:14.010
Soon, Harold's pilot had fitted Harold's sling under Pegasus.

00:20:14.720 --> 00:20:17.380
Then, Harold gently lifted him into the air

00:20:18.210 --> 00:20:21.430
and carefully carried him across the fields.

00:20:24.600 --> 00:20:29.420
When Percy saw Pegasus flying through the sky, he was amazed.

00:20:30.700 --> 00:20:34.340
Well, flatten my funnel so horses can fly after all.

00:20:34.980 --> 00:20:36.800
The children cheered for Harold.

00:20:38.100 --> 00:20:39.480
He had saved the day.

00:20:41.610 --> 00:20:44.010
Soon, Pegasus was hitched up to the cart.

00:20:47.040 --> 00:20:52.200
The party was a big success, and the children had a wonderful time.

00:20:54.440 --> 00:20:55.520
Harold was happy.

00:20:56.830 --> 00:20:59.970
He'd stayed on duty and had fun at the party too.

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:00.260
2.

00:21:33.710 --> 00:21:38.750
In the summertime, there is no better place to be than the island of Sodor.

00:21:42.440 --> 00:21:47.080
The engines are happy to show vacationers the wonderful sights to be seen.

00:21:49.210 --> 00:21:51.330
But this year, there was a problem.

00:21:53.600 --> 00:21:56.580
Thomas and Emily were in the foundry for repairs.

00:21:57.520 --> 00:21:59.980
I need to find a way to carry more passengers.

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:06.550
passengers, grumbled Sir Topham Hatt. We have more vacationers and fewer engines, said Emily.

00:22:07.560 --> 00:22:15.240
A double-decker problem, added Thomas. A double-decker problem? Hmm. This gave Sir Topham Hatt

00:22:15.240 --> 00:22:27.510
an idea. He drove straight to Bulgy's field. Bulgy is a double-decker bus. He was turned into a hen

00:22:27.510 --> 00:22:29.970
house after he caused a silly accident.

00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:43.430
accident good news bulgy i'm putting you back on the road thank you sir i'll be the best bus ever

00:22:44.990 --> 00:22:54.290
bulgy never liked being a hen house anyway the next day he went to the foundry bulgy exclaimed

00:22:54.290 --> 00:22:59.900
thomas what are you doing here i'm being repaired i'm going back on the

00:23:00.000 --> 00:23:06.620
road. I think you'll be helping the new farmer, said Emily. He needs to deliver his vegetables

00:23:06.620 --> 00:23:15.120
around the island. Vegetables? I'm going to carry passengers. Soon, Bulgy was refitted

00:23:15.120 --> 00:23:25.940
inside and out. He looked smart and shiny. Even James was impressed. Ooh. When Bulgy

00:23:25.940 --> 00:23:29.820
returned to his field, the hens thought their old house

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:30.800
Looks splendid.

00:23:32.180 --> 00:23:34.820
We'll start in the morning, said his driver.

00:23:35.180 --> 00:23:36.500
You'll stay here tonight.

00:23:37.870 --> 00:23:44.010
Bulgy was soon fast asleep, but the hens missed their old home.

00:23:44.810 --> 00:23:51.650
One by one, they crept aboard and went to sleep in the luggage racks.

00:23:52.760 --> 00:23:54.160
Bulgy knew nothing.

00:23:56.360 --> 00:23:59.460
The next morning, Bulgy picked up lots of passengers.

00:24:01.050 --> 00:24:05.920
All aboard, he tooted, and set off for the station.

00:24:06.320 --> 00:24:15.090
He was driving so smoothly that the hens didn't wake up.

00:24:20.210 --> 00:24:23.760
All was well until Bulgy turned a corner.

00:24:25.100 --> 00:24:26.980
Trevor was pulling a hay cart.

00:24:29.400 --> 00:24:29.900
Get out!

00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:42.450
of my way. He overtook Trevor. Bulgy swerved. The hens woke up. The passengers panicked

00:24:42.450 --> 00:24:49.670
and Bulgy's driver lost control. The hens were frightened. They flapped. They squawked.

00:24:50.060 --> 00:24:59.200
Stop, cried Bulgy's passengers. We want to get off. The passengers were covered in feathers

00:24:59.200 --> 00:24:59.820
and broken.

00:25:00.000 --> 00:25:07.880
eggs. They were very cross. This bus is full of hens, they complained. We shall tell Sir

00:25:07.880 --> 00:25:22.630
Topham Hatt. It's not my fault, sulked Bulgy. Sir Topham Hatt sent Bulgy to be cleaned. Silly

00:25:22.630 --> 00:25:29.940
hens, silly passengers, you can have them both. The farmer still needs help with his

00:25:30.000 --> 00:25:31.380
Vegetables, said Emily.

00:25:32.670 --> 00:25:33.890
A vegetable bus?

00:25:34.240 --> 00:25:36.480
Hmm, hey, that's not such a bad idea.

00:25:37.080 --> 00:25:40.080
And we're back carrying passengers, smiled Thomas.

00:25:41.600 --> 00:25:43.100
Bulgy is happy now.

00:25:43.560 --> 00:25:47.160
He has new green paintwork and a smart serving hatch.

00:25:49.970 --> 00:25:54.030
Sir Topham had agreed he could become the island's only vegetable stand on wheels.

00:25:56.460 --> 00:25:57.840
Bulgy likes carrying vegetables.

00:25:57.860 --> 00:25:59.730
They don't lay eggs.

00:26:00.480 --> 00:26:01.960
And they never complain.

00:26:33.680 --> 00:26:36.420
The engines love working when the sun shines.

00:26:37.380 --> 00:26:40.780
One day, Thomas and Percy were helping Salty at the docks.

00:26:41.820 --> 00:26:43.300
But Salty was worried.

00:26:44.460 --> 00:26:48.600
Arr, it may be sunny now, matey, but there be a storm coming.

00:26:51.820 --> 00:26:55.380
It may be sunny now, matey, but there be a storm coming.

00:26:58.500 --> 00:26:59.960
There be a fear storm on...

00:27:00.000 --> 00:27:06.420
the way captain peep Percy salty knew they were making fun of him he felt sad

00:27:08.820 --> 00:27:14.010
later sir Topham had arrived I want you to fetch Fergus from the smelters yard

00:27:14.010 --> 00:27:21.980
he said his driver doesn't know the line aye aye sir replied salty sadly salty

00:27:21.980 --> 00:27:27.320
was glad he was going to the smelters he didn't want to stay where he wasn't

00:27:27.320 --> 00:27:27.620
liked

00:27:30.000 --> 00:27:30.480
What's wrong?

00:27:30.730 --> 00:27:31.390
Asked Emily.

00:27:32.720 --> 00:27:36.380
Uh, nobody likes to be made fun of by silly tank engines.

00:27:37.180 --> 00:27:38.340
And he huffed away.

00:27:41.200 --> 00:27:44.620
Emily knew she had to find Thomas and Percy immediately.

00:27:48.460 --> 00:27:50.440
Those be dark clouds, matey!

00:27:50.580 --> 00:27:51.320
Whistled Thomas.

00:27:52.470 --> 00:27:54.310
There be a fierce storm on the way, Cap'n!

00:27:54.510 --> 00:27:55.150
Peeped Percy.

00:27:56.100 --> 00:27:57.220
Emily was cross.

00:27:57.840 --> 00:27:59.980
It's not nice to copy the way others speak.

00:28:00.000 --> 00:28:06.200
you heard salty's feelings we were just having fun said Percy we'll say sorry to

00:28:06.200 --> 00:28:21.470
him added Thomas but salty was nowhere to be found Thomas and Percy were worried

00:28:24.600 --> 00:28:29.600
Fergus was waiting for salty when he arrived at the smelters right on time

00:28:30.000 --> 00:28:30.840
congratulated Fergus.

00:28:31.140 --> 00:28:33.200
Aye, but there's a storm coming,

00:28:33.360 --> 00:28:34.080
said Salty.

00:28:34.180 --> 00:28:35.320
We must hurry.

00:28:35.540 --> 00:28:38.280
Soon they were hooked up

00:28:38.280 --> 00:28:39.680
and on their way home.

00:28:41.840 --> 00:28:43.860
Salty was right about the storm.

00:28:44.460 --> 00:28:44.960
It was a storm.

00:28:45.000 --> 00:28:50.900
was a fierce one. The ships at sea depend upon the lighthouse to keep them safely off

00:28:50.900 --> 00:28:54.080
the rocks. But now there was trouble.

00:29:02.300 --> 00:29:04.620
The lighthouse lamp has gone out!

00:29:04.828 --> 00:29:05.628
cried the captain.

00:29:12.476 --> 00:29:16.276
Salty and Fergus were fighting their way through the wind and rain.

00:29:18.716 --> 00:29:20.876
Then Salty saw a lantern ahead.

00:29:22.844 --> 00:29:25.064
The lighthouse keeper was waiting for him.

00:29:26.172 --> 00:29:28.172
Our lighthouse lamp has gone out!

00:29:28.188 --> 00:29:29.568
Our generator is broken.

00:29:30.508 --> 00:29:31.908
Salty had an idea.

00:29:32.556 --> 00:29:35.936
Fergus has a flywheel! It could power the generator!

00:29:36.332 --> 00:29:38.032
Hurry, shouted the lighthouse keeper.

00:29:39.884 --> 00:29:43.244
Fergus' flywheel was attached to the generator shaft.

00:29:44.716 --> 00:29:45.956
Without the lighthouse,

00:29:46.508 --> 00:29:48.808
the ship was steaming towards the rocks!

00:29:52.108 --> 00:29:54.568
Fergus was working as fast as he could.

00:29:56.204 --> 00:29:58.884
Finally, the generator came back to life!

00:30:00.636 --> 00:30:04.356
The lighthouse beams shone across the stormy sea once more.

00:30:08.668 --> 00:30:11.948
Just in time! Hard to starboard, matey!

00:30:15.132 --> 00:30:17.552
Salty's idea had saved the day.

00:30:20.092 --> 00:30:22.412
Fergus worked hard until first light.

00:30:26.236 --> 00:30:29.496
The next morning, Salty and Fergus chug back to the docks.

00:30:30.508 --> 00:30:33.048
They were surprised to see a crowd waiting for them.

00:30:33.932 --> 00:30:35.512
Thank you, said the captain.

00:30:35.788 --> 00:30:36.988
You saved our ship!

00:30:37.452 --> 00:30:38.552
Well done!

00:30:38.636 --> 00:30:39.956
Boom, Sir Topham Hatt.

00:30:41.548 --> 00:30:43.348
Salty was very proud.

00:30:43.724 --> 00:30:46.464
We're sorry if we hurt your feelings, puffed Thomas.

00:30:47.148 --> 00:30:50.148
We are only copying you because we think you're grand!

00:30:50.572 --> 00:30:54.092
Then say no more, me hearties, replied Salty happily.

00:30:55.244 --> 00:30:57.104
Now they will all work together.

00:30:57.836 --> 00:30:59.156
And have fun together.

00:31:00.000 --> 00:31:01.500
as good friends should.

00:32:00.000 --> 00:32:01.760
I saw that shadow on the wall.

00:32:02.600 --> 00:32:03.860
It's just your imagination.

00:32:04.400 --> 00:32:06.460
Look, it's just the wise old Al.

00:32:30.000 --> 00:32:33.880
And little engine wondered, he thought and thought it

00:32:34.000 --> 00:32:36.720
Really nothing's changed, it's just the same

00:32:36.720 --> 00:32:38.460
Just AI turned to night

00:32:38.830 --> 00:32:45.730
Sometimes I'll take ten

00:32:45.730 --> 00:32:47.610
And remembered the wise old Al

00:33:37.740 --> 00:33:37.980
You

00:34:09.620 --> 00:34:12.100
Look, it's just the wise old al-

00:35:00.030 --> 00:35:00.270
You
